WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:15.447
Benvolio was struggling with some of the Capulets when he heard Romeo's furious challenge to Tybalt.

2
00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:19.990
He turned around just in time to see Romeo rush after Tybalt with his sword drawn.

3
00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:25.915
News of the fight had spread quickly through Verona, and now others, including Montagues, were arriving in the

4
00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:31.560
square. Benvolio pulled Mercutio's lifeless body out of the way, then headed back to find his friend.

5
00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.073
The fight had escalated into a terrible brawl.

6
00:00:35.593 --> 00:00:39.775
Capulets and Montagues were yelling and fighting with their fists raised and swords drawn.

7
00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:43.997
Citizens of the city were grabbing at the feuding family members to keep them apart.

8
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:47.658
People were calling for the prince and his soldiers to come and restore order.

9
00:00:48.618 --> 00:00:53.240
Pushing through the crowd, Benvolio caught a glimpse of Tybalt slashing at Romeo in a far corner of

10
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:53.761
the square.

11
00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:55.241
He rushed toward them.

12
00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:58.663
When he arrived, he found his friend standing over Tybalt's body.

13
00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:03.937
Romeo was panting heavily and there was a gash on his arm, but Tybalt lay cold and still

14
00:01:03.977 --> 00:01:04.838
on the cobblestones.

15
00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:08.141
"I've killed him," said Romeo.

16
00:01:08.841 --> 00:01:12.244
Just then, they both heard a trumpet blare as soldiers arrived in the square.

17
00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:14.166
"Romeo, you must run!"

18
00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:15.547
said Benvolio.

19
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.149
"If they find you, the prince will sentence you to death."

20
00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:19.930
But Romeo didn't answer.

21
00:01:20.351 --> 00:01:23.233
Benvolio grabbed his arm and said, "Why are you waiting?

22
00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:24.514
Run! Flee!"

23
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.796
Romeo looked into his friend's eyes.

24
00:01:27.256 --> 00:01:32.612
He knew that Benvolio was right and, pausing only to hug his friend goodbye, he disappeared down an

25
00:01:32.732 --> 00:01:37.915
alley. Quickly Benvolio headed back to the main square, where the soldiers had separated the brawlers.

26
00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:42.957
The prince strode into the square and demanded, "Who is responsible for this bloodshed and disgrace?"

27
00:01:43.677 --> 00:01:44.317
"Here's one of them!"

28
00:01:44.477 --> 00:01:46.278
shouted a soldier, grabbing Benvolio.

29
00:01:46.878 --> 00:01:50.900
When he stood before the prince, Benvolio stepped away from the soldier and bowed with dignity.

30
00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:58.483
He clearly explained the entire sequence of events: how Tybalt had slain Mercutio, and how Romeo had slain

31
00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:00.104
Tybalt in revenge and then fled.

32
00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:05.071
Despite the soldiers holding them back, both families began to shout.

33
00:02:05.651 --> 00:02:10.396
The Capulets wanted Romeo's death; the Montagues pleaded for mercy and for Romeo's life.

34
00:02:11.156 --> 00:02:13.659
The prince raised his hand and the crowd went quiet.

35
00:02:13.679 --> 00:02:20.404
"I will show mercy only this far: Romeo is hereby exiled from Verona," announced the prince.

36
00:02:20.424 --> 00:02:24.508
"But the next time he is found in the city, that hour is his last."

37
00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:28.772
News of the fight and Romeo's exile spread through the city quickly.

38
00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:33.389
When the news reached the Capulet house, Lady Capulet moaned in grief at her nephew's death.

39
00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:34.890
"Oh Tybalt!

40
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.691
Tybalt!" she sobbed, and laid her head on her husband's shoulder.

41
00:02:39.231 --> 00:02:43.012
Lord Capulet tried to calm her as the nurse ran upstairs to tell Juliet.

42
00:02:43.732 --> 00:02:44.812
"What terrible news!"

43
00:02:45.132 --> 00:02:46.933
said the nurse, coming into Juliet's room.

44
00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:47.953
"He's dead.

45
00:02:48.273 --> 00:02:48.973
He's been killed!"

46
00:02:48.993 --> 00:02:51.514
"Who? Romeo?"

47
00:02:51.974 --> 00:02:55.415
gasped Juliet, still thinking of her wedding earlier that afternoon.

48
00:02:56.215 --> 00:03:00.586
Too upset to tell a long-winded story, the nurse quickly gave Juliet the heavy news.

49
00:03:00.606 --> 00:03:02.627
"No, your cousin Tybalt.

50
00:03:03.088 --> 00:03:04.729
And Romeo is banished for killing him!"

51
00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.772
Juliet was caught in a turmoil of grief.

52
00:03:08.432 --> 00:03:11.335
At first, she raged against her husband for her cousin's death.

53
00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:16.939
When she learned that Tybalt had wanted to kill Romeo, her tears of sorrow turned into tears of

54
00:03:16.999 --> 00:03:18.541
joy because he had escaped.

55
00:03:19.621 --> 00:03:23.725
Then she fell on her bed in a fresh flood of tears when she realized that she might

56
00:03:23.845 --> 00:03:25.046
never see her love again.

57
00:03:25.786 --> 00:03:27.408
The nurse didn't know how to comfort her.

58
00:03:28.144 --> 00:03:32.647
At last, she decided to leave Juliet and find Friar Lawrence in the hopes of getting a message

59
00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:33.387
to Romeo.

60
00:03:34.307 --> 00:03:39.911
Meanwhile Romeo, after making his way secretly through the streets of Verona, decided to take refuge at Friar

61
00:03:39.931 --> 00:03:40.991
Lawrence's monastery.

62
00:03:41.952 --> 00:03:45.774
There the friar bandaged Romeo's arm and told him about the prince's sentence.

63
00:03:45.794 --> 00:03:49.676
"Banishment? This is worse than death!"

64
00:03:50.256 --> 00:03:50.997
cried Romeo.

65
00:03:51.017 --> 00:03:53.438
"Heaven is here where Juliet lives!

66
00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:57.180
The world outside Verona's walls is torture─it is hell itself!"

67
00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.225
His emotions, like Juliet's, were in turmoil.

68
00:04:01.026 --> 00:04:03.988
He pulled his dagger from his belt and held it, looking at his hand.

69
00:04:04.008 --> 00:04:06.709
"This hand is cursed," he said.

70
00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:11.032
"It murdered Juliet's cousin and stained our joy with her own family's blood!"

71
00:04:11.952 --> 00:04:14.754
Just then, Juliet's nurse arrived at the monastery and knocked.

72
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:17.796
The friar answered the door and they spoke briefly.

73
00:04:18.897 --> 00:04:24.280
Without revealing that Romeo was inside, the friar promised to let Romeo know of Juliet's suffering.

74
00:04:24.948 --> 00:04:29.512
When he came back inside, he saw such a desperate look in Romeo's eyes that, for a moment,

75
00:04:30.112 --> 00:04:32.854
he was afraid Romeo might use his dagger on himself.

76
00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:35.436
"Will you kill yourself?

77
00:04:36.057 --> 00:04:37.077
Put your weapon away!"

78
00:04:37.498 --> 00:04:37.898
he said.

79
00:04:37.918 --> 00:04:40.060
"You have every reason to be happy.

80
00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.842
Tybalt tried to kill you, but you defeated him.

81
00:04:43.542 --> 00:04:48.086
By law, you should be sentenced to death, but the prince softened your sentence to banishment.

82
00:04:48.906 --> 00:04:50.968
And Juliet is alive and calling for you."

83
00:04:51.976 --> 00:04:55.018
At the thought of Juliet, Romeo stood up and put his dagger away.

84
00:04:55.718 --> 00:05:00.922
Friar Lawrence told him to visit his love that night, as they had originally planned, but warned him

85
00:05:00.962 --> 00:05:03.063
to escape to nearby Mantua before morning.

86
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:07.946
"When the time is right, I'll announce your marriage and joyfully reconcile your families.

87
00:05:08.706 --> 00:05:13.489
Then the prince cannot refuse to pardon you, and you can return," he explained.

88
00:05:13.509 --> 00:05:16.431
"While you're away, I'll send letters with news."

89
00:05:17.391 --> 00:05:22.199
So that night, when Romeo snuck into the garden where he and Juliet had first vowed their love,

90
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.062
he found a ladder hidden just where they had planned.

91
00:05:25.722 --> 00:05:29.325
He climbed up, and Juliet happily welcomed him onto her balcony.

92
00:05:29.946 --> 00:05:34.810
Together, they smiled for the first time since the horrible events in the city square that afternoon.

93
00:05:36.091 --> 00:05:42.216
Downstairs in the front hall, Juliet's parents were just saying goodbye to Paris, the count who wanted to

94
00:05:42.256 --> 00:05:42.997
marry Juliet.

95
00:05:43.017 --> 00:05:46.320
"Juliet won't come down tonight," said Lady Capulet.

96
00:05:47.296 --> 00:05:49.097
"She is too distraught over Tybalt's death."

97
00:05:49.857 --> 00:05:51.998
"These are sad times," said Paris.

98
00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:55.900
"My wife will talk to my daughter in the morning," Lord Capulet said.

99
00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:59.221
"I promise you, in three days, the two of you will marry."

100
00:05:59.241 --> 00:06:03.543
"I thank you," said Paris, and they shook hands before saying goodnight.

101
00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:08.425
As dawn approached, the birds began to chirp and the sky grew lighter in the east.

102
00:06:09.185 --> 00:06:11.046
Romeo knew it was time for him to leave.

103
00:06:11.066 --> 00:06:12.486
"Will you go?"

104
00:06:12.926 --> 00:06:13.587
said Juliet.

105
00:06:14.247 --> 00:06:17.908
She also knew it was time for Romeo to leave, but she couldn't bear to part.

106
00:06:17.928 --> 00:06:19.729
"The day isn't near.

107
00:06:20.189 --> 00:06:22.730
That bird you heard was the nightingale, not the lark.

108
00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.690
It sings in our garden every night."

109
00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:27.031
Romeo smiled.

110
00:06:27.051 --> 00:06:29.232
"Oh believe me, love," she said.

111
00:06:29.252 --> 00:06:30.612
"It was the nightingale."

112
00:06:30.632 --> 00:06:34.533
"It was the lark," said Romeo, "the herald of the morning."

113
00:06:35.153 --> 00:06:37.034
But Romeo too did not want to leave.

114
00:06:37.054 --> 00:06:43.576
"Together, dear Juliet, we'll pretend that the sun doesn't brighten the clouds in the east, but some strange

115
00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:44.436
meteor instead.

116
00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.963
Let me be captured and put to death, as long as I never have to say goodbye."

117
00:06:49.643 --> 00:06:54.827
At these words, Juliet remembered the danger he faced, and her longing suddenly changed to fear.

118
00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:57.168
She threw her arms around his neck.

119
00:06:57.709 --> 00:06:58.409
"It was the lark!

120
00:06:58.749 --> 00:07:00.731
The stars have gone and the sky grows light!

121
00:07:01.191 --> 00:07:01.971
Oh, you must go!"

122
00:07:03.032 --> 00:07:05.954
Romeo stepped to the ladder and climbed over the balcony's rail.

123
00:07:05.974 --> 00:07:07.895
"Farewell, farewell.

124
00:07:08.696 --> 00:07:12.979
One kiss, and I'll descend," he said, and their lips touched one last time.

125
00:07:13.559 --> 00:07:16.404
Then, without a word, Romeo climbed down and was gone.
